From ec4852dc02c6da2376dc6a81bea845980db47669 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mecattaf <thomas@mecattaf.dev>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:30:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Expose validated native drag lifecycle to desktop shells

Queue pointer drag lifecycle events through the existing outbound writer. Provide a bounded, desktop-pinned JSON stream for shell pointer-capture policy.

Validate with core fmt/clippy/tests, all 942 compositor unit tests, and an actual cross-application Wayland drag through Imagine into Kitty.

Guidelines audited: TESTING, ERRORS, CONTROL_FLOW, FUNCTIONS, FILES, WRITING, RUST, DATA, DISCRIMINATED_UNIONS and OPTION_RESULT. The compositor integration fixture that reassigns HOME remains excluded by the session runtime-isolation requirement.
